VALUES (587, '3', $t$ASK 587: a judge is not removed for a defect of the engine's own making (form fixes of run 42071, A to E)$t$,
  $t$A judge is not sent back, counted, or removed for a defect of the engine's own making, and a judge's RESULT is not raised to a challenger win past a counted challenger break. Five such defects were found in run 42071: the 1,500-character cut and the splice; the own-words check; the keystone label that cannot exist; the second reading reversing the first; the RESULT written as CHALLENGER WINS beside a counted challenger break. A real fault of the same kind is still raised. (plan rev 3, section 1)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the card "Write ASK 587" pressed 23:17 CST 2026-11-23 in W4's thread, with no run live (last execution 42071) (Wall 11360; audit 41171). One write of the engine and the child together: engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 196402d0 to 7536d7bf-06ad-44b1-b852-aaab6388ee2c (Shared Library d749630c to 752887af, 1,174,075 characters; Reread Record 3f7bdf9e to 9d506a0f; Alt Reread Record e56f5714 to 4283a2e0); child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT f900375e to a7113b8d-3379-48ce-944c-a40f6f4eb5c9 (Shared Library 6d92bf4e to 3159ff7d; R2 Alt Reread Record 36a70121 to f6e6bbaa). Items: A the checks read the judge's whole line, not the 1,500-character copy (A3: a cut-marked line makes no E-COL item); B the own-words check; C1 the keystone label; C2 the second reading; D the counted unnamed challenger break reaches every RESULT path (the v25 line, the v61 tag, the gate recompute) and the standing rule (LIB 1345) is unchanged; E no UNREAD COUNTED LINE from a send-back item line. W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11361): versionId and activeVersionId 7536d7bf and a7113b8d; 0 nodes differ from the graded targets; only the five planned nodes changed against the prior live; no model setting or credential changed; library sha f45effef8ec77157 in both. IN PART, because every EXPECT line A to E is unexercised until a run holds its case (plan section 8). Shown offline only: t586 40 PASS, ALL PASS, rerun by W1; the built sbApply2024 run on stored judgment 1273 (live CHALLENGER WINS, target UNDERDETERMINED); the scope check (engine 64 sources 93 uses, child 62 sources 92 uses, 0 out of scope). The plan went through four revisions: rev 0 graded by W1 with D failed (F1, as the plan states of Wall 11330); rev 1 and rev 2 each returned on D (Wall 11342 F1, Wall 11354 D4, as the plan states); rev 3 PASS (Wall 11357), in which W1 withdrew its own 11354 F2 as a mistake of reading scope in plain LIB order. Stated limit of D (plan section 3 item 7): a false closing-contradiction flag now also blocks CHALLENGER WINS on BROKEN. Split out of this ASK to their own: B1 (ASK 550 line), B3 (gemini's three results), B4 (gate refusal counted UNCURED), and G1 to G8 for the operator. RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). A, C2 and E are shown as the paths that fired; B, C1 and D are UNEXERCISED. In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
